course: dictionary
lesson: 13511
title: Impaired: weakened or damaged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Impaired» means weakened, damaged or not working as well as normal. The verb is «impair», which means to make something work less well. Context helps: if a sentence is about eyes, ears or thinking, impaired is probably about how well something works.
explain: «Mia is visually impaired, so she reads books with large print.» Visually impaired means having poor sight. «Sam is hearing impaired and uses a hearing aid.» Hearing impaired means having poor hearing. These are respectful ways to talk about people who have sight or hearing loss.
explain: Impaired can also describe thinking and choices. «The driver's judgement was impaired by tiredness.» Tiredness, alcohol or looking at a phone can weaken judgement, so a person may not make safe choices. Ask yourself: what has been weakened? Then swap in your own meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Impaired means weakened, damaged or not working as well as normal.
fact: To impair something is to damage it or make it work less well.
fact: «Visually impaired» means having poor sight.
fact: «Hearing impaired» means having poor hearing.
fact: «Impaired judgement» means weaker thinking and decision-making, for example after tiredness, alcohol or using a phone while driving.
exercise: «Mia is visually impaired.» What does visually impaired mean? | Being very good at drawing | Having a very loud voice | *Having poor sight | Living near the sea
exercise: «The driver's judgement was impaired by tiredness.» What does impaired mean here? | Completely finished | Painted bright red | *Weakened, so it does not work as well | Made stronger and faster
exercise: Find the word that is the verb in «Loud music can impair your hearing over time.» | music | loud | time | *impair
test: «Sam is hearing impaired, so he uses a hearing aid.» What does hearing impaired mean? | Liking loud music | *Having poor hearing | Being unable to speak | Wearing a hat
test: «Using a phone while driving can impair a driver's judgement.» What does impair mean? | *To damage something or make it work less well | To drive very fast | To make something brighter | To fix something completely
exam: «Tiredness, alcohol and phones can all impair judgement, so a driver should stay alert.» What does impair mean? | To paint something | To make a loud noise | To count quickly | *To weaken or damage something
